@title Postmortem: late sales dashboards
@subtitle Analytics Platform · Juniper Retail · 2026-10-02

# Impact

- 9 hours of delay
- 23 dashboards stale
- The 08:00 executive sales report went out with the previous day's numbers

# Pipeline

diagram pipe dir=LR title="Daily sales pipeline"
pipe: db "Orders DB" db
pipe: cdc "CDC Connector" svc
pipe: kafka "Kafka" queue
pipe: spark "Spark Job" fn "failed with out-of-memory" focus
pipe: wh "Warehouse" store
pipe: dash "Dashboards" svc
pipe: db -> cdc
pipe: cdc -> kafka
pipe: kafka -> spark : orders topic
pipe: spark -> wh
pipe: wh -> dash

# Timeline

table = Time,Event; 01:00,nightly Spark Job starts; 01:47,Spark Job fails with out-of-memory on the orders partition for 2026-10-01; 02:30,automatic retry also fails; 07:55,analyst reports stale dashboards; 08:20,on-call doubles executor memory to 16 GB and reruns; 10:05,Spark Job succeeds; 10:58,dashboards refreshed

# Root cause

A promotion produced 3.4 times the normal order volume: 4.1 million orders against a typical 1.2 million. Executors had 8 GB each, which was not enough for that volume.

# Lessons learned

## What went well

- The retry was scheduled automatically.
- On-call reran the job within 25 minutes of the analyst report.

## What did not

- Nobody was paged after the retry failed.
- Dashboards gave no sign that the data was stale.
- Executor memory was sized for normal volume, not for a promotion.

# Action items

1. Page on-call when the nightly job fails twice.
2. Size executor memory from the input volume.
3. Add a data freshness banner to dashboards.
